# Backend (NestJS)

- Business logic lives in NestJS services, not controllers.
- State changes for workflows go only through the future WorkflowService (when implemented); do not scatter transitions.
- External messaging (SMS, push) goes only through provider/outbox abstractions — not ad-hoc direct sends from controllers.
- Controllers remain thin: validate input, call services, map responses.
- NestJS is the only trusted business-logic layer for operational writes.
